[0.055, "o", "\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[38;2;167;139;250m◆\u001b[39m  \u001b[1mJudgment\u001b[22m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  2 tools judged · hardened fields (9) · schemas inferred (4)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \u001b[33m⚠ 1 advisory string clamped (over-long or unusable) — tool judgments were unaffected\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  Tiny repo — I read every file. Only three route files exist: app/api/accounts/route.ts,\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  app/api/transfer/route.ts, and the Vendo wire catch-all. app/page.tsx is a static <h1>Maple</h1> with no\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  server actions, and there is no lib/, no middleware, no data layer.\r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  accounts: a two-line GET returning a hardcoded array literal. Graded read — no stored state, no request\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  input at all (the signature is GET(), it never touches Request). The response is a BARE ARRAY, not a {\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  data: [...] } envelope, so I wrote the outputSchema that way; an agent binding to an envelope here would\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  break. balanceCents is minor units (429900 = $4,299.00).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  transfer: destructures fromId/toId/amountCents out of the JSON body and answers { ok: true, ...echo }. Two\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  things worth a human's attention. First, the honest state of the code: this handler persists nothing and\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  calls nothing — it is an echo stub, so on a literal reading of \"does stored state change\" it changes none.\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  I still graded it write with confirmEach, because the contract the tool exposes IS inter-account money\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  movement and it reports ok:true for it; an agent that calls this believes funds moved, and the persistence\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  gap is an implementation hole rather than a benign-tool signal. Grading a transfer endpoint read would let\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  the policy's \u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;167;139;250mrisk: read -> run\u001b[39m\u001b[22m rule fire transfers unattended the moment a DB write lands behind it. If you\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  disagree, this is the one grade to revisit — the code, quoted above, is all there is.\r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  Second, and suspicious: neither handler has ANY auth. No session lookup, no cookie or bearer check, no\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  ownership check tying fromId to the caller. /api/transfer will move money for whoever can POST to it, and\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  it never verifies the caller owns fromId. I deliberately left audience unset rather than assert \"end-user\"\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  — there is no auth in the source to read, so any audience I sent would be a guess dressed up as evidence.\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  Please set it once real session lookup exists. Also note the Vendo wire route hardcodes principal: () => ({\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  kind: \"user\", subject: \"demo-user\" }), which is the shipped demo placeholder, and .vendo/brief.md is still\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  the untouched template prompt — so nothing in this repo currently distinguishes one caller from another.\r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  No enums or closed-set fields appear anywhere in the source, so I sent none.\r\n\r\u001b[2K"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \u001b[33m⚠ missed surface (not extracted yet): app/api/vendo/[...vendo]/route.ts — a catch-all exporting\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \u001b[33mGET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE from nextVendoHandler(vendo) that produced zero tools. I believe this is correct:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \u001b[33mit is Vendo's own transport/control plane, not maple-bank product surface, and grading a catch-all at its\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \u001b[33mworst reachable operation w…\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[2K"]
